name: Investigation refresh preserves saved selection and explains unavailable history
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/campaign_selection.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: campaign held
require-live-snap: 25 held-1 | held-investigation
nav-mode:
keys: Down Enter
require-live-snap: 20 held-2 | selected-job
keys: End
require-live-snap: 20 held-2 | original-reading-position
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/campaign_selection.py @TMP_TARGET @ART insert
keys: r
require-live-snap: 20 held-2 | inserted-history-keeps-selection
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/campaign_selection.py @TMP_TARGET @ART reorder
keys: r
require-live-snap: 20 held-2 | reordered-jobs-keep-selection
ask: Does refresh preserve the same investigation, selected job and reading position after earlier history appears and unapproved job rows are reordered, without launching work?
resize: 160x48
keys: End
live-snap: selected-job-160x48
expect: held-2
resize: 96x89
keys: End
live-snap: selected-job-96x89
expect: held-2
resize: 80x24
keys: End
live-snap: selected-job-80x24
expect: held-2
resize: 60x20
keys: End
live-snap: selected-job-60x20
expect: held-2
resize: 40x12
keys: End
live-snap: selected-job-40x12
expect: held-2
ask: Can the selected recorded job and return controls remain readable across all six sizes while resize preserves its identity?
resize: 60x20
keys: NPage
live-snap: paged-before-refresh
keys: r
live-snap: paged-after-refresh
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/campaign_selection.py @TMP_TARGET @ART paging
ask: Does refresh retain the same positive reading offset after ordinary PageDown, while keeping return controls visible?
resize: 120x36
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/campaign_selection.py @TMP_TARGET @ART remove
keys: r
require-live-snap: 20 Previously selected campaign | unavailable-selection
expect: Choose a campaign to inspect
ask: When the selected history is unavailable, does the browser explain the loss and return to selection instead of displaying another job through the old reader?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/campaign_selection.py @TMP_TARGET @ART verify
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
